# Forest snail (#329, D106): native 24x16 frames, facing right, sole on row 15. A chestnut shell coiled in two turns
# (dark groove s, lit whorls t/S, cream highlight c); its ink contour covers only the top two rows of the shell, below
# that the shell edge is the light lip o, so the moon rim caps the shell and the snail measures like the spider (D106).
# The foot and neck (f, u, F) keep their own colour as the edge; the stalks end in pale eyes e; m is the mouth.
# crawl1, crawl2: the crawl; look, blink: the notice (stalks up, pulled in); draw: the wind-up (reared, throat
# swollen); spit: thrust forward; rest: the reload (head low); dead: the empty shell on its back, mouth open upward.
# gob: the gob's two 8x8 wobble frames (fly1 at x 0, fly2 at x 8) in the cell's top-left; the rest of the cell is empty.
# The concept was generated from shapes for the author's review (#329); this grid is now the drawing, edited by hand.
